WEBVTT

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:13.200
It's almost time.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.200
Wait!

00:00:14.510 --> 00:00:16.070
Hey, wait up!

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:18.870
Come on! Pick up the pace!

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:21.080
You're going too fast, Matsuri-chan!

00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:23.920
Let's go!

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:26.060
Wait!

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:27.500
What's the rush?

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:46.980
Isn't she with General Affairs?

00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:54.400
Bingo!

00:01:19.510 --> 00:01:22.140
Public Safety and General Affairs in cahoots?

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:23.760
What's the world coming to?

00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:31.460
Judging from the thickness, it's around two million yen.

00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:33.420
That's some pretty cheap "justice."

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:37.380
Well, if this goes public, the Katahira Faction will fall apart.

00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:41.680
Yakumo's gonna be happy.

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:42.200
Huh?

00:03:57.730 --> 00:03:58.750
One, two!

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:05.640
Every day feels just like every other day
onaji you ni naraberareta hibi

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:12.640
And in them I can't taste any bitter or sweet
amasa mo nigasa mo kanjinai

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:21.650
With ourselves, with our pain still deep within my heart
bokura wa itami wo mune ni daita mama de

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:26.610
I can try again to fly
mou ichido toberu

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:27.280
Good.

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:27.770
I can try again to fly
mou ichido toberu

00:04:27.770 --> 00:04:29.990
All right! I'm off!

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:36.710
The lights are coming together from a future reaching out to me
temaneku mirai kara hikari ga atsumatte

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:37.570
May my voice reach you, from my heart to wherever you are
kimi no moto he boku no koe yo todoke

00:04:37.570 --> 00:04:39.320
See you later.

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:42.220
May my voice reach you, from my heart to wherever you are
kimi no moto he boku no koe yo todoke

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:51.060
No matter how sad the nights are, I can still believe
donna ni kanashii yoru datte shinjirareru yo

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:57.400
I love the whole world and want to tell you
taisetsu na kono sekai kara omoi wo

00:04:58.520 --> 00:04:59.770
How I feel
tsutaetai

00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:05.640
It's morning, Yuuki.

00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:07.280
How long are you gonna stay in bed?

00:05:09.010 --> 00:05:10.740
Don't go back to sleep!

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:13.640
Your adorable childhood friend is here to wake you!

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:16.860
You're supposed to get up with your heart racing!

00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:18.290
Hey, come on!

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:22.160
Oh, you're not gonna listen, huh?

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:22.960
All right, then.

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:30.540
Well? Give up yet?

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:35.200
Come on, we'll be late for our morning meeting.

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:36.940
Now wake up and—

00:05:43.450 --> 00:05:45.490
Mifuyu!

00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:47.280
Good morning!

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:48.940
Good morning.

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:51.020
You two are always together.

00:05:51.020 --> 00:05:52.540
You get along like bread and butter.

00:05:52.540 --> 00:05:55.000
More like butter and a <i>knife</i>.

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:57.480
Wow, that must hurt. Did Chisato do that?

00:05:57.480 --> 00:05:59.600
I did it because Yuuki showed me something weird.

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:00.790
You think I <i>wanted</i> to?!

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:03.320
Are you okay, Yuu-kun?

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:05.520
Abracadabra.

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:07.800
Pain, pain, go away!

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:13.380
Mii-chan!

00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:14.820
There, there.
Mii-chan!

00:06:14.820 --> 00:06:15.380
Mii-chan!

00:06:15.380 --> 00:06:18.420
You're so kind, unlike Chisato.

00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:19.400
What'd you say?!

00:06:19.990 --> 00:06:21.320
All right. That settles it!

00:06:22.590 --> 00:06:24.560
Mii-chan, I love you.

00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:26.060
Will you go out with me?

00:06:26.060 --> 00:06:26.660
What?

00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:30.340
I'm serious. I want to go out with you!

00:06:30.340 --> 00:06:33.230
Yuu-kun, I'm flattered,

00:06:33.230 --> 00:06:36.120
but I'm in love with someone else.

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:36.910
Impossible!

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:39.300
Too bad, Yuuki.

00:06:39.300 --> 00:06:42.880
You should've noticed your feelings for her earlier.

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:44.420
Now it's too late.

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:45.420
Oh, no!

00:06:45.730 --> 00:06:49.570
Cheer up. I'm sure that someday you'll find

00:06:49.570 --> 00:06:51.390
the love of your life.

00:06:52.790 --> 00:06:54.760
Can we go now?

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:56.140
Yeah.

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:02.560
It's been a while since we performed a skit like that.

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:04.520
It's not something we should do in the middle of town.

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:06.980
You started it.

00:07:08.930 --> 00:07:10.570
Oh, nobody's here—

00:07:12.730 --> 00:07:14.740
G-Good morning, Morishita-san.

00:07:14.740 --> 00:07:16.900
Good morning, Oojima.

00:07:16.900 --> 00:07:18.900
You're here early today.

00:07:18.900 --> 00:07:19.800
Normal.

00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:21.380
Are you looking for something?

00:07:21.380 --> 00:07:22.080
Normal.

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:24.500
Right, completely norm—

00:07:24.950 --> 00:07:28.300
This obviously isn't "normal"! What part of her are you talking to?

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:29.760
Good morning, Morishita-san.

00:07:30.170 --> 00:07:32.660
Um... what are you doing?

00:07:36.550 --> 00:07:37.310
Pink.

00:07:38.490 --> 00:07:41.880
Pink? Chisato, you're wearing pink today?

00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:44.140
No, it's a sky-blue thong—

00:07:44.140 --> 00:07:45.900
Like hell I'll tell you!

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:48.570
Good morning, everybody!

00:07:48.570 --> 00:07:53.660
Oh, my! Yuu-chan, did you do something wrong that warranted scolding again?

00:07:53.660 --> 00:07:55.440
No, it's just a misunderstanding—

00:07:55.440 --> 00:07:57.700
You never learn, do you, Ooshima?

00:07:57.700 --> 00:08:00.040
You're so dumb, Ooshima.

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:01.620
I didn't do anything.

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:04.460
And my name is Oojima, not Ooshima.

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:06.790
It doesn't really matter, Ooshima.

00:08:06.790 --> 00:08:09.180
It's all the same to me, Ooshima.

00:08:09.180 --> 00:08:09.920
It's not the same!

00:08:09.920 --> 00:08:12.780
People's names are important!

00:08:12.780 --> 00:08:13.780
Yeah, yeah.

00:08:13.780 --> 00:08:14.780
Ah!

00:08:17.570 --> 00:08:19.200
Non-chan left her latest invention,

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:24.260
the self-sustaining, super high-speed, starch saccharification and solidification device,

00:08:24.260 --> 00:08:26.190
a.k.a. "Ametako Mk. 3," turned on!

00:08:26.530 --> 00:08:28.440
Non-chan, are you all right?

00:08:29.830 --> 00:08:32.600
Good morning, Yuuki-senpai.

00:08:33.570 --> 00:08:38.080
Wow, the Food Club's filled with snacks today! Looks fun!

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:41.000
That's a disturbing way to describe this disaster.

00:08:46.010 --> 00:08:47.900
Are these all new flavors?

00:08:47.900 --> 00:08:48.340
Yes, I proudly present these Umachin-brand snacks.

00:08:48.340 --> 00:08:50.840
Umachin

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:52.980
You're so lucky.

00:08:52.980 --> 00:08:56.700
When you go home, you have an all-you-can-eat supply of your company's snacks.

00:08:56.700 --> 00:08:59.760
Whoever marries Yume gets to share this privilege, Ooshima!

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:01.620
Why tell <i>me</i> that?

00:09:01.620 --> 00:09:02.780
Nice one.

00:09:02.780 --> 00:09:06.880
So what do you think, Yuuki-senpai?

00:09:06.880 --> 00:09:07.800
About what?

00:09:07.800 --> 00:09:09.520
What? Weren't you listening?

00:09:10.050 --> 00:09:14.030
You can eat my Yaoi Stick at your leisure.

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:16.280
Well, how should I put this?

00:09:16.280 --> 00:09:17.160
However and wherever.

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:21.040
All right, all right. Enough about Yume's marriage.

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:23.910
Let get down to taste-testing these new Yaoi Sticks.

00:09:24.750 --> 00:09:25.800
Excuse me.

00:09:25.800 --> 00:09:28.700
Let's begin with number one, as usual.

00:09:30.990 --> 00:09:31.960
Ready, go!

00:09:32.950 --> 00:09:34.400
It's white.

00:09:34.400 --> 00:09:35.480
Sure is.

00:09:37.340 --> 00:09:39.350
It's delicious!

00:09:39.350 --> 00:09:43.200
Wow, that looked just like a TV commercial.

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:45.100
We got two great smiles.

00:09:46.330 --> 00:09:47.850
How is it, Morishita-san?

00:09:49.670 --> 00:09:50.610
Normal.

00:09:51.370 --> 00:09:53.570
I see. "Normal."

00:09:53.570 --> 00:09:55.320
I'll try one, too.

00:09:57.510 --> 00:10:00.040
What are you looking at, Yumeshima-kun?

00:10:00.040 --> 00:10:03.900
Yuuki-senpai putting my Yaoi Stick in his mouth.

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:07.090
Ouch, that hurt!

00:10:07.090 --> 00:10:09.210
Wh-What are you doing?

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:10.840
Let's have a taste.

00:10:10.840 --> 00:10:11.380
Hey!

00:10:20.870 --> 00:10:23.720
This is white chocolate-flavored.

00:10:24.230 --> 00:10:26.760
I'm sorry. It slipped my mind.

00:10:26.760 --> 00:10:28.730
The President doesn't like chocolate, does she?

00:10:29.170 --> 00:10:32.340
Don't worry. I'm just picky.

00:10:32.340 --> 00:10:37.740
You're in the Food Club, but you can't eat chocolate. I feel bad for you, Chii-chan.

00:10:37.740 --> 00:10:39.660
Yeah, I feel bad.

00:10:39.660 --> 00:10:40.910
Yeah, so unfortunate.

00:10:41.980 --> 00:10:43.700
You don't seem all that sympathetic.

00:10:46.630 --> 00:10:47.900
Thanks.

00:10:47.900 --> 00:10:48.710
Yeah.

00:10:49.550 --> 00:10:51.210
Big news! Big news, everyone!

00:10:51.950 --> 00:10:55.170
What's the matter, Hazuki-sensei?
You're out of breath.

00:10:55.670 --> 00:10:59.010
Let me get a quick drink first.

00:11:09.230 --> 00:11:11.560
Nothing better than a morning round!

00:11:12.870 --> 00:11:14.970
Um... Sensei?

00:11:14.970 --> 00:11:15.880
What?

00:11:15.880 --> 00:11:18.600
Oh, worried over me drinking this early?

00:11:18.600 --> 00:11:22.570
It's all right. If I could get fired for something like this, I would've been fired already.

00:11:22.950 --> 00:11:25.320
So what's the big news, Hazuki?

00:11:25.320 --> 00:11:26.580
Oh, yeah.

00:11:28.050 --> 00:11:29.760
There we go.

00:11:30.950 --> 00:11:33.110
Well, this club...

00:11:33.110 --> 00:11:34.880
might get disbanded!

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:35.710
What?

00:11:36.190 --> 00:11:38.040
Disbanded?!

00:11:38.040 --> 00:11:38.980
Yup.

00:11:48.210 --> 00:11:50.040
And that concludes my report.

00:11:50.040 --> 00:11:52.980
That's it?! Take some responsibility!

00:11:52.980 --> 00:11:56.480
Silence. Silence please.

00:11:56.480 --> 00:11:57.660
Chairman.

00:11:57.660 --> 00:11:59.400
Tatsumi Moheiji-kun.

00:11:59.890 --> 00:12:02.980
Hello. I'm General Affairs Commissioner Tatsumi Moheiji.

00:12:02.980 --> 00:12:05.370
I would like to inquire about the Oosawa Incident—

00:12:06.070 --> 00:12:09.780
specifically, Public Safety Commissioner Oosawa's exuberant interrogation of the suspect

00:12:09.780 --> 00:12:12.670
and the information leak that caused the upsurge of

00:12:13.170 --> 00:12:16.040
harassment towards financial aid students.

00:12:16.470 --> 00:12:21.200
You promised for a full investigation of this incident and a recovery plan

00:12:21.200 --> 00:12:24.050
but have yet to fulfill that duty.

00:12:24.050 --> 00:12:28.380
The former public safety commissioner who appointed Oosawa-kun as his successor

00:12:28.380 --> 00:12:31.430
was you, Student Council President Mouri.

00:12:31.430 --> 00:12:36.940
The responsibility for appointing her is <i>very</i> heavy.

00:12:37.390 --> 00:12:40.230
Maybe it's best that you <i>resign immediately</i>.

00:12:40.230 --> 00:12:41.820
He's right!

00:12:43.450 --> 00:12:44.500
Objection!

00:12:47.490 --> 00:12:49.420
Forgive my tardiness.

00:12:49.420 --> 00:12:51.680
I was looking into something.

00:12:51.680 --> 00:12:53.620
May I have the floor?

00:12:53.620 --> 00:12:55.620
Shinonome Satsuki-kun.

00:12:56.110 --> 00:12:57.670
Shinonome!

00:12:57.670 --> 00:13:00.760
I am Finance Commissioner Shinonome Satsuki.

00:13:00.760 --> 00:13:03.020
I have a question for the General Affairs Commissioner.

00:13:03.020 --> 00:13:06.040
Do you know who would be the next president

00:13:06.040 --> 00:13:09.430
if the Student Council President were to resign immediately?

00:13:09.770 --> 00:13:15.420
W-Well, I believe the Vice-President would be the acting president until the next election.

00:13:15.420 --> 00:13:20.190
I see. And are you aware of what the current president's main duty is?

00:13:20.510 --> 00:13:23.900
That would be to transfer duties to the next administration...

00:13:24.450 --> 00:13:28.820
Wouldn't it be difficult for an inexperienced vice-president to transfer those duties?

00:13:29.390 --> 00:13:34.330
Do you not feel that the President's resignation would be a loss for the school?

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:37.880
B-But the Public Safety Commission, with which the President is affiliated,

00:13:37.880 --> 00:13:41.190
has many other issues and unaccounted expenditures.

00:13:41.190 --> 00:13:42.440
Th-That's...

00:13:42.440 --> 00:13:45.420
This is an inventory that I borrowed from the General Affairs Commission.

00:13:45.420 --> 00:13:48.840
<i>She must have done that before coming here.</i>

00:13:49.270 --> 00:13:53.140
The freshman in charge kindly showed it to me.

00:13:53.140 --> 00:13:54.200
According to this,

00:13:54.200 --> 00:13:57.270
the same kind of expenditures are also present in the General Affairs—

00:13:57.270 --> 00:14:00.240
Well, these aren't really unaccounted!

00:14:00.240 --> 00:14:03.720
The details will be filled sometime soon. It's just...

00:14:03.720 --> 00:14:08.440
If you don't mind, I would like to return to the original topic and report the settlement.

00:14:08.440 --> 00:14:10.640
W-Well, I suppose that's fine.

00:14:10.640 --> 00:14:14.040
The future of the school management is more important than the past!

00:14:15.770 --> 00:14:17.040
Did you hear?

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:19.920
About the next presidential election, I mean.

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:22.920
What's this I hear about a bunch of clubs getting disbanded?

00:14:23.490 --> 00:14:25.670
That's Finance Commissioner Shinonome Satsuki!

00:14:26.070 --> 00:14:31.680
Her campaign manifesto is about cutting down on the needlessly ample number of clubs!

00:14:32.100 --> 00:14:34.840
Clubs without achievements would face budget cuts and disbandment

00:14:34.840 --> 00:14:38.600
to reduce overall school expenditures.

00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:40.980
This is a huge problem!

00:14:40.980 --> 00:14:43.300
The Action Figures Club that I'm in

00:14:43.300 --> 00:14:47.520
needs a large budget for the cost of silicone rubber that's used to make models.

00:14:47.520 --> 00:14:53.490
There's also the urethane cast used for mass production, and the table used for the booth

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:55.800
in the cultural festival held twice a year!

00:14:55.800 --> 00:14:56.500
Come again?

00:14:56.990 --> 00:15:02.220
We're making models, the so-called "garage kits."

00:15:02.220 --> 00:15:04.440
So that's why your nickname's Garage?

00:15:04.440 --> 00:15:05.090
Indeed.

00:15:05.630 --> 00:15:07.440
I've been meaning to ask, but...

00:15:07.440 --> 00:15:11.360
Is that propeller thing on your
head one of those "garage kits" too?

00:15:11.360 --> 00:15:12.550
Huh? Propeller?

00:15:13.090 --> 00:15:16.060
No, I don't have a propeller.

00:15:17.430 --> 00:15:18.680
What's going on?

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:19.580
What's up?

00:15:19.580 --> 00:15:21.600
Actually, forget about it.

00:15:21.990 --> 00:15:24.620
We FNOS also have full color,

00:15:24.620 --> 00:15:28.840
dawn pink, coating paper and stamping, flyleaf and weaving, et cetera.

00:15:28.840 --> 00:15:30.030
They all cost a lot.

00:15:30.550 --> 00:15:33.450
The Food Club also uses a lot for buying snacks.

00:15:33.450 --> 00:15:37.680
And we just eat them without achieving a single thing.

00:15:37.680 --> 00:15:40.910
We couldn't really object if we were on the disbandment block.

00:15:40.910 --> 00:15:42.250
We could!

00:15:42.250 --> 00:15:43.940
If the Food Club's gone,

00:15:43.940 --> 00:15:48.400
who would I say "It's delicious"
to whenever I eat a snack?

00:15:48.400 --> 00:15:51.090
The Finance Commissioner hasn't been elected yet.

00:15:51.090 --> 00:15:54.050
But she probably will. She's popular.

00:15:54.050 --> 00:15:55.430
She's got big boobs.

00:15:55.430 --> 00:15:56.680
She's beautiful.

00:15:56.680 --> 00:15:57.890
She's got big boobs.

00:15:57.890 --> 00:15:59.180
She's reliable.

00:15:59.180 --> 00:16:00.560
She's got big boobs!

00:16:01.330 --> 00:16:05.460
And even if she got elected, that doesn't mean she would follow up on her manifesto, right?

00:16:05.460 --> 00:16:07.740
She probably would.

00:16:07.740 --> 00:16:09.690
She's serious about stuff like that.

00:16:09.690 --> 00:16:13.740
Hazuki-sensei, do you know the Finance Commissioner?

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:16.860
Yeah. I mean, she's my sister, you know.

00:16:16.860 --> 00:16:17.900
What?!

00:16:17.900 --> 00:16:18.270
You didn't know?

00:16:18.270 --> 00:16:19.240
I'm all out.
You didn't know?

00:16:19.240 --> 00:16:21.400
They're totally different!

00:16:21.400 --> 00:16:23.750
She's like, so organized and perfect, you know?

00:16:24.150 --> 00:16:26.420
Well excuse me for not being perfect.

00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:28.630
But it's true that she's my sister.

00:16:29.190 --> 00:16:30.180
You're right.

00:16:30.180 --> 00:16:32.130
The boobs say it all.

00:16:32.130 --> 00:16:35.010
Hazuki, if she's your sister, can't you talk to her?

00:16:35.010 --> 00:16:38.720
No way. She's stubborn, unlike me.

00:16:38.720 --> 00:16:41.380
Darn. Then what should we do?

00:16:41.380 --> 00:16:43.520
How about we support another candidate?

00:16:43.910 --> 00:16:47.720
If it's not a candidate from the General Affairs, Finance, or Public Safety Commissions,

00:16:47.720 --> 00:16:49.900
they might not even pass the primaries.

00:16:50.290 --> 00:16:55.660
Public Safety's a no-go since Commissioner Oosawa lost her position from that scandal.

00:16:55.660 --> 00:16:59.450
Then only that <i>thing</i> from General Affairs is left.

00:16:59.450 --> 00:17:01.100
General Affairs...

00:17:01.100 --> 00:17:01.950
..."thing"?

00:17:01.950 --> 00:17:06.330
That's correct! I am General Affairs Commissioner Tatsumi Moheiji.

00:17:06.710 --> 00:17:08.960
Wh-What the hell?

00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:11.360
Is that what we were talking about yesterday?

00:17:11.360 --> 00:17:13.590
There's no other alternative.

00:17:13.590 --> 00:17:15.840
But <i>that</i> is not acceptable.

00:17:15.840 --> 00:17:18.380
A student council president shouldn't be masked.

00:17:18.380 --> 00:17:19.460
What mask?

00:17:19.460 --> 00:17:20.470
Look.

00:17:21.350 --> 00:17:23.300
He's not wearing a mask.

00:17:23.300 --> 00:17:26.730
No, it's not <i>that</i> kind of mask. I mean the one that's covering his face.

00:17:26.730 --> 00:17:30.610
He definitely isn't handsome, but calling it a "mask" is going too far.

00:17:30.610 --> 00:17:33.740
<i>What's going on? Am I the only one who can see it?</i>

00:17:33.740 --> 00:17:36.760
<i>Garage's propeller, too. Is there something wrong with my eyes?</i>

00:17:37.240 --> 00:17:38.220
Whoa!

00:17:38.220 --> 00:17:42.820
Please lend me, Tatsumi Moheiji, your support in the upcoming election.

00:17:44.890 --> 00:17:48.790
Isn't this... a prepaid card for the school store?

00:17:48.790 --> 00:17:52.240
Yes. It's worth only 100 yen,

00:17:52.240 --> 00:17:54.050
but it's the thought that counts.

00:17:55.010 --> 00:17:56.900
Isn't this bribery?

00:17:56.900 --> 00:17:58.930
Bribery? How so?

00:17:58.930 --> 00:18:02.810
Aren't you distributing these so that people vote for you?

00:18:02.810 --> 00:18:06.360
I have not said anything to imply that!

00:18:06.360 --> 00:18:09.540
It's just a sign of my appreciation.

00:18:09.540 --> 00:18:13.660
Please lend me, Tatsumi Moheiji, your support in the upcoming election.

00:18:13.660 --> 00:18:16.040
Hey, give us some.

00:18:16.040 --> 00:18:18.660
Oh, yes! My apologies!

00:18:18.660 --> 00:18:21.650
Please lend me, Tatsumi Moheiji, your support...

00:18:21.650 --> 00:18:24.320
Seriously... Isn't that against the rules?

00:18:24.320 --> 00:18:29.300
No, the election hasn't officially been announced yet, so it's not.

00:18:29.300 --> 00:18:30.400
No way!

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:32.940
I-I can't... stop...

00:18:32.940 --> 00:18:35.380
Please make way!

00:18:37.840 --> 00:18:38.840
Yuuki!

00:18:38.840 --> 00:18:39.590
Are you okay?

00:18:40.590 --> 00:18:42.110
Ouch...

00:18:42.110 --> 00:18:44.640
I-I'm sorry. Are you okay?

00:18:44.640 --> 00:18:47.460
I couldn't stop while running down the slope.

00:18:47.460 --> 00:18:49.600
I'm sorry. Are you hurt?

00:18:50.350 --> 00:18:53.340
No, I'm fine. Are <i>you</i> all right?

00:18:53.340 --> 00:18:56.540
I'm fine. I'm so sorry. Really.

00:18:56.540 --> 00:18:59.000
No, it's no big deal.

00:18:59.000 --> 00:19:01.680
But weren't you in a hurry?

00:19:01.680 --> 00:19:02.450
Ah...

00:19:04.950 --> 00:19:06.960
I'm really sorry.

00:19:09.470 --> 00:19:11.460
What are you staring at?

00:19:12.110 --> 00:19:14.720
She must be a financial aid student.

00:19:14.720 --> 00:19:15.360
Eh?

00:19:16.940 --> 00:19:19.960
You're right. That's a courtesy bus for financial aid students.

00:19:19.960 --> 00:19:22.090
She must work in a factory after school.

00:19:22.090 --> 00:19:24.420
That's why she was in a hurry.

00:19:29.170 --> 00:19:31.720
Did she drop this?

00:19:31.720 --> 00:19:34.160
Thank you very much!

00:19:34.160 --> 00:19:37.650
Please! Please lend me, Tatsumi Moheiji, your support...

00:19:38.270 --> 00:19:42.500
In any case, I don't want to vote for that Tatsumi Moheiji guy!

00:19:42.500 --> 00:19:43.400
I agree.

00:19:43.400 --> 00:19:46.240
A candidate who uses dirty tricks is unacceptable!

00:19:46.670 --> 00:19:48.160
Then we're in a bind.

00:19:48.160 --> 00:19:50.000
There aren't any other strong candidates.

00:19:50.370 --> 00:19:51.880
So that's it, huh?

00:19:51.880 --> 00:19:53.500
Not necessarily.

00:19:53.810 --> 00:19:57.250
If there's no other candidate, why don't you guys run?

00:19:57.250 --> 00:20:01.300
There's no point. Even if we do, we can't possibly win—

00:20:01.300 --> 00:20:03.510
Are you fine with the Food Club being disbanded?

00:20:05.230 --> 00:20:08.740
It's either waiting for the Food Club to be disbanded

00:20:08.740 --> 00:20:11.140
or putting your hopes on a slight chance.

00:20:12.730 --> 00:20:16.260
If there's no other way, I don't think you've got anything to lose.

00:20:16.260 --> 00:20:19.160
I'd hate to lose a place where I could get a quick drink.

00:20:21.070 --> 00:20:22.150
All right.

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:24.910
I'm not gonna sit back and wait to get crushed.

00:20:24.910 --> 00:20:26.830
We've got nothing else to lose!

00:20:26.830 --> 00:20:28.370
We'll run against the Finance Commissioner!

00:20:28.370 --> 00:20:32.080
Non-chan concurs! The Food Club must go on!

00:20:32.080 --> 00:20:33.620
I'm in, too!

00:20:33.620 --> 00:20:36.330
She's not doing whatever she wants just 'cuz she's got big boobs!

00:20:36.330 --> 00:20:39.460
I'll lend you guys a hand, too.

00:20:39.460 --> 00:20:43.760
Me, too. I'll do whatever it takes to protect this place.

00:20:46.010 --> 00:20:47.100
Michiru?

00:20:47.670 --> 00:20:50.180
Will you fight with us, Michiru?

00:20:51.790 --> 00:20:54.440
If Oojima will, then I will, too.

00:20:56.350 --> 00:21:00.030
Hear that, Yuuki? What about you?

00:21:00.030 --> 00:21:01.360
Well...

00:21:03.250 --> 00:21:04.340
Of course!

00:21:04.340 --> 00:21:05.860
I'm with you all the way!

00:21:06.310 --> 00:21:08.120
Then it's unanimous.

00:21:17.330 --> 00:21:18.580
I'll take the bottom.

00:21:20.290 --> 00:21:22.510
Let me in, too!

00:21:23.010 --> 00:21:26.840
We're all in this together! For the future of the Food Club!

00:21:26.840 --> 00:21:28.010
Yeah!

00:21:32.530 --> 00:21:36.420
First, we'd better decide on our candidate.

00:21:36.420 --> 00:21:37.770
Who's running?

00:21:40.130 --> 00:21:40.760
What?

00:21:41.630 --> 00:21:43.030
Me?!

00:21:50.910 --> 00:21:52.160
Soon,

00:21:52.710 --> 00:21:54.660
the election will begin.

00:21:56.390 --> 00:22:00.160
What should I do, Kana?

00:23:42.730 --> 00:23:44.580
Isn't it weird that "homemade" chocolates

00:23:44.580 --> 00:23:47.760
are just melted and reshaped chocolate bars?

00:23:47.760 --> 00:23:49.720
There's no homemade feel to that.

00:23:49.720 --> 00:23:52.860
Actually, Non-chan-senpai makes it from cacao liquor, cocoa butter,

00:23:52.860 --> 00:23:56.410
sugar, lactose, vegetable oils, milk extracts, and emulsifier all mixed together!

00:23:56.410 --> 00:23:57.840
Sounds professional.

00:23:57.840 --> 00:24:01.360
And then I fold it over heat with gelatinizer and polysaccharide thickener.

00:24:01.360 --> 00:24:03.420
That wouldn't harden, would it?

00:24:03.420 --> 00:24:05.580
Next time, Episode 2: "Running!"

00:24:05.580 --> 00:24:10.980
Fold, fold, fold it to death!
